 r←GetPackageDescription packagePath;cfg;qdmx
⍝ Returns the "description" of the package in `packagePath`, or '' when it has none.
⍝ A package published before the field existed simply has nothing to say, and that is no
⍝ reason to make a fuss: the page then carries no description either.
 r←''
 :Trap 11 19 22 Reg.ErrorNo
     cfg←Reg.GetPackageConfigFileAsNS packagePath
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     LogError'Cannot read the package config in "',packagePath,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
     :Return
 :EndTrap
 :If 0<cfg.⎕NC'description'
     r←cfg.description
 :EndIf
